---
source: crates/odx-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: cmd.render_long_help().to_string()
---
Record a verdict or mute about a suggestion of `odx suggest`

Usage: odx verdict add [OPTIONS] --addon <ADDON> --kind <KIND> --reason <REASON> <CHANGE>

Arguments:
  <CHANGE>
          The suggestion: `<owner>/<repo>#<n>` or `orphaned_commits`

Options:
      --addon <ADDON>
          The addon it is about

  -C, --project-dir <DIR>
          Run as if started in DIR

  -c, --config <FILE>
          The pyproject.toml or repos.yaml to use

      --target <SERIES>
          The series it is judged for (default: the project's)

      --from <SERIES>
          The series the suggestion came from, when several have it

  -j, --jobs <N>
          Override the number of parallel jobs

      --kind <KIND>
          Kind of verdict

          Possible values:
          - not-applicable:  The change does not apply to the target series
          - not-needed:      The change is not needed on the target series
          - superseded:      Superseded by another change
          - already-present: Already present on the target, possibly by another route
          - declined:        Declined for this project
          - not-wanted:      Not wanted in this project
          - deferred:        Review later; re-checked on expiry and on target code changes

      --offline
          Serve forge and index data from the cache only. Only network calls are skipped: local work (git, pre-commit, odoo-lint) takes as long as before

      --fresh
          Ignore cached data; refresh everything before answering

      --reason <REASON>
          Why; mandatory

      --no-refresh
          Use cached data even when stale. Like --offline, this saves network time only

      --scope <SCOPE>
          Scope; the default depends on the kind

          Possible values:
          - environment:  One environment of this project
          - project:      Every environment of this project
          - organisation: Every project of the organisation

      --env <ENV>
          Environments of an environment-scope mute

      --refresh-index
          Rebuild the addon index for the series involved

      --json
          Machine-readable output on stdout

      --until <DATE>
          Expiry date (YYYY-MM-DD)

      --no-recheck
          Do not resurface when the target code changes

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase log verbosity (repeatable)

  -q, --quiet
          Errors only

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
